I chose strong opposite weights on the velocity for the left (action 0) and right (action 2) actions so that the policy reacts decisively to the sign of the car’s velocity, which is the key driver for gaining momentum in MountainCar. The left action has large negative velocity weight (‑6.0) and a modest negative position weight (‑1.0) to push the car left when it’s moving left or far from the goal. The right action mirrors this with positive weights (1.0 for position, 6.0 for velocity) to accelerate right when the velocity is positive. The “no‑acceleration” action is kept neutral (zero weights) with a slight negative bias (‑2.0) so it is chosen only when neither left nor right strongly dominate, preventing wasteful inaction. All values are within the allowed range and differ by steps of about 1.0 from typical baseline values, enabling exploration of a policy that could reach the goal in far fewer than 200 steps.
